    explanation: 'Class imbalance for rare event detection: (1) The accuracy paradox: accuracy is a misleading metric when classes are imbalanced, 99% accuracy is achieved by always predicting the majority class, completely failing at the detection task; (2) Correct metrics for imbalanced classification: Precision-Recall AUC (AUC-PR), F1-score, Cohen\'s Kappa, Matthews Correlation Coefficient: NOT accuracy, NOT ROC-AUC alone (ROC curves are less informative under severe imbalance); (3) Techniques: Class weights (set class_weight to balanced or custom weights), most computationally efficient; SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique), generates synthetic minority examples by interpolating between existing ones; Undersampling (NearMiss, ENN), reduces majority class; Threshold tuning, lower decision threshold from 0.5 to optimize recall/precision tradeoff; (4) Business metric alignment: in fraud detection, a false negative (missed fraud) costs much more than a false positive, use asymmetric cost matrix; (5) Vertex AI AutoML handles class imbalance automatically with class weight options. Source: Google Professional ML Engineer exam guide, Chawla et al. (2002) SMOTE.',
