    explanation: 'Differential Privacy in ML: (1) Problem, trained models can memorize training examples; membership inference attacks can determine if a specific record was in the training set, leaking privacy; (2) DP-SGD (Differentially Private Stochastic Gradient Descent), adds calibrated Gaussian noise to per-example gradients before aggregation, with a privacy budget (epsilon, delta); (3) Guarantee, with (ε, δ)-DP, the probability of inferring any individual\'s inclusion in training data is bounded; (4) Trade-off, lower epsilon (stronger privacy) → more noise → lower accuracy; (5) TensorFlow Privacy implements DP-SGD. Source: Google MLE, Responsible AI documentation.',
